  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Let $P=QR.$ What is the value of ${p}_{31}$, if\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\n${p}_{31}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying the $3$rd row in $Q$ by the $1$st column in $R$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}_{31} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2(5)+1(-3)+(-2)(1) \\\\  & =10-3-2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
